 * sibling spokes src/pages/screed-isolation.astro, src/pages/acoustic-underlay.astro
 * and src/pages/sports-track-underlay.astro — same class helpers, progressive-
 * enhancement scroll-reveal motion, hand-rolled breadcrumb and combined JSON-LD
 * @graph (prefix `as-`).
 *
 * ─── ROUTING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The content entry src/content/products/acoustic-strips.yaml carries
 * `path: /acoustic-strips` (child of the `acoustic` hub — already listed in that
 * hub's `children`). To avoid a duplicate-route build error the matching branch
 * is filtered out of getStaticPaths in src/pages/[...slug].astro — the same
 * pattern already used for acoustic-underlay, sports-track-underlay,
 * screed-isolation, zainfit, zainsquare, zainduo, zainactive-rolls and
 * curb-stone. The YAML entry stays as data (still referenced by the acoustic
 * hub nav / children list); this file serves the URL.
 *
 * ─── DECISIONS TAKEN / FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 "Data Integrity" + §6) ─────────
 *  - PARENT HUB: the build request's breadcrumb JSON-LD names the parent
 *    "Acoustics & Construction Systems" at /acoustics-construction-systems on
 *    host rukanalzain.com. That route does not exist in this project — the real
 *    acoustic hub is /acoustic-soundproofing-flooring (acoustic-strips.yaml
 *    `hub: acoustic`, and the hub already lists this page under `children`).
 *    Both the visible breadcrumb and the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD below use the
 *    real path with the label "Acoustic & Soundproofing Flooring" — the same
 *    substitution already made on the acoustic-underlay, sports-track-underlay
 *    and screed-isolation siblings. TODO: confirm the intended hub label / slug
 *    with the client.
 *  - CANONICAL HOST: the request shows "rukanalzain.com"; the configured site is
 *    "ruknalzain.ae" (astro.config.mjs). Canonical + all schema URLs are
 *    built from the configured site via BaseLayout `canonical={PATH}` (same
 *    choice as the siblings). TODO: confirm the production domain.
 *  - DESIGN SYSTEM: the request describes React / Lucide-React / a generic
 *    Tailwind palette. This is a static Astro site (zero-JS). The page follows
 *    the live charcoal / industrial-grey design system with a single amber
 *    action accent and bordered "ghost" WhatsApp buttons; Lucide icons are
 *    inlined as raw SVG path data (no runtime). The FAQ accordion uses native
 *    <details>/<summary>.
 *  - H1 / METADATA: the request's H1 ("Zain Acoustic Strip — Perimeter &
 *    Decking Isolation Dubai") and title/description supersede the shorter copy
 *    in acoustic-strips.yaml ("Zain Acoustic Strip — Self-Adhesive Vibration
 *    Isolation"), the same way the sibling pages diverged from their YAML
 *    records. The YAML stays as-is for the hub nav.
 *  - TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS: acoustic-strips.yaml lists Width options (mm),
 *    Thickness (mm) and Roll length (m) as null "to collect". Every spec row
 *    rendered below is the descriptive text supplied in the page-build request,
 *    NOT numeric data from Rukn_Al_Zain_SEO_Content_Brief V2.docx. Treat as
 *    PROVISIONAL and confirm against real product data / manufacturer
 *    certificates before go-live.
 *  - STRUCTURED DATA: a single combined @graph (BreadcrumbList + Product +
 *    FAQPage) is emitted inline. The request supplied BreadcrumbList only; the
 *    FAQPage node is generated 1:1 from the on-page FAQ and the Product node is
